<title>USA: U.S. mortgage application volume fell in latest wk.</title>
<headline>U.S. mortgage application volume fell in latest wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The volume of U.S. mortgage applications fell 3.8 percent in the week ended May 16, according to a Mortgage Bankers Association of America weekly survey.</p>
<p>Specifically, the volume of applications to refinance mortgages rose 9.6 percent in the latest survey week, while applications to purchase mortgages fell 6.9 percent.</p>
<p>The seasonally adjusted refinancing index rose 9.6 percent to 332.5 from 303.4 the previous week.</p>
<p>The purchase index fell 6.4 percent to 192.0 in the latest survey from 205.1 in the previous week.  </p>
